### Goal Model Decomposition

The mission is decomposed into a hierarchical goal model where each goal is defined with its type, decomposition, runtime annotation, and justification. The model is structured to reflect the sequential execution of collection and delivery phases, with parallel execution of tasks within each phase and fallback mechanisms for battery constraints.

#### Goals

| Goal ID | Goal Title | Goal Text | Goal Type | Target Condition | Runtime Annotation | Relation | Justification |
|--------|------------|-----------|-----------|------------------|-------------------|----------|----------------|
| G1     | Fulfill Resource Request | Deliver required resources to the requesting agent | Achieve | All resources delivered to the specified location | ; (sequential) | AND | The mission requires both collection and delivery to fulfill the request. These phases must be executed sequentially. |
| G2     | Collection Phase | Collect required resources from storage locations | Achieve | All resources collected from their respective storages | # (parallel) | AND | Multiple robots can collect from different storages in parallel to reduce mission time. |
| G3     | Delivery Phase | Deliver collected resources to the specified location | Achieve | All resources delivered to the specified location | ; (sequential) | AND | Delivery can only begin after all resources are collected. |

#### Tasks

| Task ID | Task Title | Task Text | Relation | Location | Number of Robots | Justification |
|---------|------------|-----------|----------|----------|-------------------|----------------|
| AT1.1   | Collect from Storage 1 | Collect resources from Storage 1 | AND | Storage 1 | 1 | Each storage is a separate task, executed by one robot. |
| AT1.2   | Collect from Storage 2 | Collect resources from Storage 2 | AND | Storage 2 | 1 | Each storage is a separate task, executed by one robot. |
| AT2.1   | Deliver to Destination | Deliver resources to the specified location | AND | Destination | 1 | A single delivery task, executed by one robot. |

### Logical Relationships

- **G1 -> G2, G3 [AND; sequential]**
  - **Justification**: The mission requires both collection and delivery phases to be executed sequentially to fulfill the resource request.

- **G2 -> AT1.1, AT1.2, ... [AND #]**
  - **Justification**: Each storage location must be collected from, and these tasks can be executed in parallel by different robots to reduce mission time.

- **G3 -> AT2.1 [AND]**
  - **Justification**: The delivery phase involves a single task to deliver all collected resources to the destination, executed sequentially after collection.

### Summary

The goal model is structured to ensure that the mission is executed efficiently, with parallel collection tasks and sequential delivery. Fallback mechanisms are integrated into each task to handle battery constraints, ensuring mission resilience.
